9. Testing Strategy
Testing is an important part of the development process.
The project uses automated unit tests to validate individual components and methods.
The testing process includes:
1.	Identifying the functionality to test.
2.	Preparing test data.
3.	Executing the required method.
4.	Comparing actual and expected results.
5.	Recording the test outcome.
6.	Fixing issues when tests fail.
7.	Re-running tests to verify corrections.
The use of automated testing helps reduce regression issues and improves overall application reliability.
